    "rationale": "Dilution experiments reveal the undiluted readings significantly underestimate biomass in the final hours. At t=18h: undiluted reading was 0.673, but a 10× dilution yielded 0.3501 (implying true undiluted equivalent of ~3.5 OD600). A 2× dilution at the same timepoint gave 0.6881 instead of the expected ~0.337, indicating non-proportional behavior. This pattern was confirmed at t=14h (2× dilution: 0.6633 vs undiluted 0.6899). The non-linearity is explained by cell clumping/aggregation in stationary phase—high-density cultures form cell aggregates that scatter light disproportionately, causing optical density readings to plateau while actual biomass continues to be present. The proportional response at 10× dilution suggests the biomass is ~5.2× higher than the undiluted readings indicate."
